      "motion_identity": "Exactly TWO walking legs, TWO muscular arms and TWO separate RED bat wings. Preserve the pale athletic body, ivory skull-like face, TWO original dark curved horns, dark waist cloth, dark feet and claws. CRITICAL ASYMMETRY: the SINGLE CHARCOAL BRACER covers ONLY the creature RIGHT forearm, seen on the VIEWER LEFT in INPUT1. It stays on that SAME anatomical arm in EVERY pose in BOTH near-front directions, remaining on viewer LEFT; the viewer RIGHT forearm stays PALE and uncovered. Never mirror the whole figure, swap the bracer, put it on both arms, remove it or turn just the head. Correct complete left-facing AND right-facing bodies, face/chest/knees/toes aligned together, compact grounded two-foot steps with restrained bob. Preserve the athletic torso and leg lengths; no purple skin, new tail, weapon or armor from INPUT2.",
